    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "If $\\overset{\\to }{u}=⟨6,-2⟩$, $\\overset{\\to }{v}=⟨-2,-3⟩$ and $\\overset{\\to }{w}=⟨3,-1⟩$, then $2\\overset{\\to }{u}-(2\\overset{\\to }{v}+3\\overset{\\to }{w})=$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\overset{\\to }{u}-(2\\overset{\\to }{v}+3\\overset{\\to }{w}) &= 2\\cdot ⟨6,-2⟩-(2\\cdot ⟨-2,-3⟩+3\\cdot ⟨3,-1⟩) \\\\ &= ⟨2\\cdot 6-(2\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 3),2\\cdot (-2)-(2\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot (-1))⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨12,-4⟩-(⟨-4,-6⟩+⟨9,-3⟩) \\\\ &= ⟨12,-4⟩-⟨5,-9⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨12-5,-4-(-9)⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨7,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
