    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "If $\\overset{\\to }{u}=⟨6,-4⟩$, $\\overset{\\to }{v}=⟨3,4⟩$ and $\\overset{\\to }{w}=⟨-4,5⟩$, then $4\\overset{\\to }{u}-(2\\overset{\\to }{v}-3\\overset{\\to }{w})=$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\overset{\\to }{u}-(2\\overset{\\to }{v}-3\\overset{\\to }{w}) &= 4\\cdot ⟨6,-4⟩-(2\\cdot ⟨3,4⟩-3\\cdot ⟨-4,5⟩) \\\\ &= ⟨4\\cdot 6-(2\\cdot 3-3\\cdot (-4)),4\\cdot (-4)-(2\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 5)⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨24,-16⟩-(⟨6,8⟩-⟨-12,15⟩) \\\\ &= ⟨24,-16⟩-⟨18,-7⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨24-18,-16-(-7)⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨6,-9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/id": "4f72e7c8-7e2b-59e6-8b0a-e06fbc6008a3",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
